{"title":"The Tyranny of the Alphabet 2","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/973825589/0/marginalrevolution~The-Tyranny-of-the-Alphabet.html","date":1795436259000,"content":"<p>I wrote about the <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2006/04/the_tyranny_of_.html\">Tyranny of the Alphabet</a> many years ago. In economics the standard then was to list authors alphabetically:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>Faculty members in top departments with surnames beginning with letters earlier in the alphabet are substantially more likely to be tenured, be fellows of the Econometric Society, and even win Nobel prizes (let’s see, Arrow, Buchanan, Coase…hmmm). No such effects are found in psychology where the alphabetical norm is not followed.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>The tyranny is still with us. The AEA now lets coauthors certify a random order with the ⓡ symbol, as in <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/aer.20161492\">Ray ⓡ Robson</a>, but alphabetical order remains the norm.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.cantgetmuchhigher.com/\">Chris Dalla Riva</a> has a <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.cantgetmuchhigher.com/p/the-alphabet-broke-the-grammys\">nice example of alphabetical tyranny from the Grammys</a>. From 2021 to 2025 the Grammys basically listed nominees alphabetically (the details are a bit messy see Dalla Riva for the full story), and lo and behold nominees with starting names beginning with A,B,C, D or E won suspiciously more than one would expect compared to the share of such names in the Billboard charts.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies.webp\"><img src=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies-1024x759.webp\" alt=\"Grammy win rates by alphabetical position of nominee, 2021 to 2025 compared with other years\" width=\"1024\" height=\"759\" srcset=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies-1024x759.webp 1024w, https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies-300x223.webp 300w, https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies-768x570.webp 768w, https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grammies.webp 1440w\" /></a></p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html\">The Tyranny of the Alphabet 2</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/973825589/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/973825589/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/973825589/marginalrevolution,https%3a%2f%2fmarginalrevolution.com%2fwp-content%2fuploads%2f2026%2f11%2fgrammies-1024x759.webp\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/973825589/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/973825589/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/973825589/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comment-161092061\">In reply to Phil S..   The prime minister of Hungary is named ...</a> <i>by Peter</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comment-161091937\">Winners of the best English play awards from 1590-1605 (the ...</a> <i>by copans</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comment-161091926\">Is there not some ethnic bias inherent in alphabetizing?</a> <i>by Pshrnk</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comment-161091923\">In reply to Fergus.   I only comment here to say: look for me ...</a> <i>by Brent Buckner</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comment-161091919\">In reply to Phil S..   Yes, we don't see people in the US with ...</a> <i>by mkt42</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/94257.html#comments\">Plus 10 more...</a></li></ul></div><h3>Related Stories</h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/the-ai-gains-that-gdp-misses.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=the-ai-gains-that-gdp-misses\">The AI gains that gdp misses</a></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/still-unproven-can-britain-build-a-tunnel.html?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=still-unproven-can-britain-build-a-tunnel\">Still Unproven: Can Britain Build a Tunnel?</a></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/will-ai-growth-reach-the-developing-world.html?ut